venv/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
archive/

# The total tool's draws files (tools/estimate_total.py --draws) are rebuilt exactly from the table at its seed, so they are not committed; the JSON beside them is (roadmap item 2.55, 2026-11-12).
**/results/estimate_total_draws/

# The pinned Quarto, installed per working tree by tools/quarto_setup.py from the release tarball checked against tools/house_format/quarto.toml; 420 MB, rebuilt by that command, so never committed (layout migration step 1, 2026-11-13).
vendor/

# Each typeset draft's PDF under its numbered name (tools/typeset.py, tools/document_names.py); the PDF committed beside its source is the same bytes, so a committed number's PDF is found in history by its log's commit (roadmap item 2.66, 2026-11-13).
**/documents/drafts/

# A reader pilot's text parts are rebuilt exactly from the committed stored texts by its make_pilot.py, so they are not committed (efficacy_angle_well_designed/pilot/pilot.md 3.5); ignored so the owner's editor does not list them as changes (2026-11-08).
cases/*/reviews/*/pilot/texts/*/*.txt

# A new-client test run's sealed session transcripts hold the owner's address and are never committed unscrubbed (notes/new_client_test.md 7.6, 8.7); ignored so the owner's editor does not list them as changes (2026-11-09, after he saw "32 files uncommitted").
trials/new_client_test/*/transcripts/

# A user's API keys live in the env block of their local Claude Code settings, never in the repository (.claude/skills/scope-case/SKILL.md 3.9); Claude Code ignores it on its own only where it wrote the file itself (2026-11-10).
.claude/settings.local.json

# A publisher's subscription copy, read under the owner's library access and not for redistribution; the case may be shared, so its PDF and full text stay on this machine only (the coordinator's instruction of 2026-11-12).
cases/*/sources/sharma_2023_threat_net/original.pdf
cases/*/sources/sharma_2023_threat_net/text.txt
cases/*/sources/sharma_2023_threat_net_supplement/original.zip
cases/*/sources/sharma_2023_threat_net_supplement/text.txt
research/sources/bastos_2010_validating_gp_thesis/original.pdf
research/sources/bastos_2010_validating_gp_thesis/text.txt

# The pinned Quarto, installed per working tree by tools/quarto_setup.py from the release tarball checked against tools/house_format/quarto.toml; 420 MB, rebuilt by that command, so never committed (layout migration step 1, 2026-11-13).
vendor/

# Each typeset draft's PDF under its numbered name (tools/typeset.py, tools/document_names.py); the PDF committed beside its source is the same bytes, so a committed number's PDF is found in history by its log's commit (roadmap item 2.66, 2026-11-13).
**/documents/drafts/

# Test clients' case folders (stored sources, 40 to 120 MB a run, 0.9 GB in all), kept on this machine: the conversations and counts are committed, and the case folders are ignored so the owner's editor does not list them. The drivers copied into a run folder are scratch scripts.
trials/new_client_test/*_half_*/case/
trials/new_client_test/*/nct_driver*.py
trials/new_client_test/*/case/results/model/draws_*.npz

# Empty read-only placeholders the Claude Code sandbox puts at the root over paths it protects; they hold nothing of the project's and must never be committed. A real file at one of these paths needs its line removed first.
/.bash_profile
/.bashrc
/.gitconfig
/.gitmodules
/.idea
/.mcp.json
/.profile
/.ripgreprc
/.vscode
/.zprofile
/.zshrc
/.claude/commands
/.claude/hooks
/.claude/launch.json
/.claude/loop.md
/.claude/output-styles
/.claude/routines
/.claude/workflows

# Owen's Monte Carlo book chapter 8 is the author's online draft, each page saying 'do not distribute or post electronically without author's permission'; its PDF and full text stay on this machine only (research/refs.toml entry `owen_2013_monte_carlo_ch8`, 2026-11-17).
research/sources/owen_2013_monte_carlo_ch8/original.pdf
research/sources/owen_2013_monte_carlo_ch8/text.txt
